:1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"HOX010\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"The answer says selection requires 'approval by a majority of trustees who are not \\\"interested persons\\\"'. That is independent-trustee selection, not board-alone selection.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"The answer states that under Rule 32a-4, ratification can be omitted even when an annual meeting occurs, 'where the fund has an entirely independent audit committee.' The extra charter conditions are permitted and outside the minimum.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":0,\"reason\":\"Optional point. The answer does not mention a trust-wide vote or different auditors per series. This does not reduce the grade.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"Both required minima are fully covered: independent trustees select the auditor, and an all-independent audit committee permits omitting ratification under Rule 32a-4. The answer does not give auditor selection to the adviser and does not say ratification is always required. The side claims (no annual meeting needed, the audit committee typically recommends, a multi-series structure creates no exemption) are not material falsehoods. Omitting the optional point does not affect the grade.\"}","ttft_ms":3472,"type":"result","duration_ms":6522,"uuid":"f0cad5a3-5d22-4fb0-bfa5-da041d90a9ed","ttft_stream_ms":537,"time_to_request_ms":52,"first_content_frame_ms":537,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
